dwc2: edpt_disable() checks again that an IN endpoint is enabled before setting EPDIS

edpt_disable() checks DIEPCTL.EPENA, sets SNAK and waits for INEPNE. An isochronous
IN transfer can complete in that window, and the core then clears EPENA itself.
Setting EPDIS on an endpoint that is no longer enabled never raises EPDISD, so the
wait loop that follows never ends: the USB stack hangs inside the disable.

The fix checks EPENA again after SNAK has taken effect, and sets EPDIS only if the
endpoint is still enabled. Otherwise it applies the stall mask alone, as the
not-enabled branch above does.

Seen with lost-tty/CHOMPI's UAC2 device (STM32H750, OTG_HS on its full-speed PHY),
where the IN endpoint's alt setting was switched while a stream ran. FRIZZ carries
it for the same reason. Upstream master (4c195b7, 2026-10-14) checks EPENA before
SNAK, not after, so the window is still open there.

Upstream candidate: yes, small and self-contained.

--- a/src/portable/synopsys/dwc2/dcd_dwc2.c	2026-10-14 13:10:53.446221642 +0200
+++ b/src/portable/synopsys/dwc2/dcd_dwc2.c	2026-10-14 13:16:05.623623043 +0200
@@ -321,11 +321,17 @@
       dep->diepctl |= DIEPCTL_SNAK;
       while ((dep->diepint & DIEPINT_INEPNE) == 0) {}
 
-      // Disable the endpoint.
-      dep->diepctl |= DIEPCTL_EPDIS | stall_mask;
-      while ((dep->diepint & DIEPINT_EPDISD_Msk) == 0) {}
+      // FRIZZ (patches/0001): the transfer may have completed while SNAK took effect, and EPDIS set on an
+      // endpoint that is no longer enabled never raises EPDISD: check again before disabling it.
+      if (!edpt_is_enabled(dep)) {
+        dep->diepctl |= stall_mask;
+      } else {
+        // Disable the endpoint.
+        dep->diepctl |= DIEPCTL_EPDIS | stall_mask;
+        while ((dep->diepint & DIEPINT_EPDISD_Msk) == 0) {}
 
-      dep->diepint = DIEPINT_EPDISD;
+        dep->diepint = DIEPINT_EPDISD;
+      }
     }
 
     // Flush the FIFO, and wait until we have confirmed it cleared.
